# Day 19

1. Expert
Experts are smaller neural networks inside a larger model. Each expert learns different patterns during training and get specialized for that particular topic.

2. Router 
Routing is the process of deciding which experts should process a particular token.
The router examines the token’s hidden representation and assigns scores to the available experts.

3. Active Parameters
Suppose an MoE model has:
 100 billion total parameters.
 10 experts.
 10 billion parameters activated for a particular token (illustrative).
The model has 100 billion parameters in total but it doesn’t use all of them for every token. It activates only a subset.

MoE architectures can provide substantial model capacity without requiring every parameter to participate in every token’s computation.
Fewer active parameters do not necessarily mean lower memory requirements.

MoE (Mixture of Experts)
It Efficiently assigning tokens to experts, Stors large expert weights.
Moves tokens between GPUs when experts are distributed. Prevents a few experts from receiving too many tokens so they don't get halocinate.

